1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,987
Hi, this is Gemihub Hybrid: local answers, connected communities.

2
00:00:04,987 --> 00:00:17,325
Our existing platform, gemihub, already lets independent neighborhood shops create their own bespoke websites and booking pages simply by chatting with AI, with no templates and no web agency needed.

3
00:00:17,325 --> 00:00:19,950
A town guide then connects those shops together.

4
00:00:19,950 --> 00:00:30,862
Here is the problem: once a shop publishes its site, sending every routine question like opening hours to a cloud LLM creates unpredictable traffic costs for a small business.

5
00:00:30,862 --> 00:00:43,087
For Build Hybrid AI 2026, I extended gemihub with a Firebase AI Logic hybrid inference layer for both the town guide and shop assistants, with no visitor API keys required.

6
00:00:43,900 --> 00:00:50,637
On supported Chrome devices, standalone questions about a single shop's published facts use prefer on-device mode.

7
00:00:50,637 --> 00:01:03,175
Gemini Nano answers directly in the browser, and the badge reports the real inference source from the Firebase AI Logic SDK: On-device, with zero cloud inference cost for common FAQs.

8
00:01:03,990 --> 00:01:17,177
When a visitor compares multiple shops, asks follow-ups, or exceeds our input threshold, our routing policy switches to cloud-only mode with Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite, protected by Firebase App Check.

9
00:01:17,177 --> 00:01:23,952
Both the cloud model and input limits can be tuned live via Firebase Remote Config without redeploying.

10
00:01:24,750 --> 00:01:29,675
Inside Robata Akari's own assistant, the same handoff happens in one chat.

11
00:01:29,675 --> 00:01:34,837
First, opening hours are answered On-device using only this shop's published facts.

12
00:01:34,837 --> 00:01:37,525
Next, booking a table switches to Cloud.

13
00:01:37,525 --> 00:01:47,637
Existing deterministic MCP tools verify live availability and pricing, and the confirmation modal ensures the model never confirms a reservation on its own.

14
00:01:48,440 --> 00:01:55,290
And if a visitor's browser doesn't support Gemini Nano, or while the model is still downloading, chat never blocks.

15
00:01:55,290 --> 00:02:00,227
Firebase AI Logic falls back cleanly to the cloud and labels it honestly.

16
00:02:00,227 --> 00:02:06,152
Try the live demo at hybrid dot gemihub dot net, and check out our MIT-licensed code on GitHub.

17
00:02:06,152 --> 00:02:07,302
Thanks for watching!
